@startuml
title SABLE — Baseline-to-Candidate Obligation Analysis
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
actor Developer
participant "SABLE Analyzer" as SABLE
participant "HCL Parser / Extractor" as HCL
participant "Registered Obligation" as BASE
participant "Candidate Correspondence" as CORR
participant "Authorization Projection" as AUTH
database "Evidence Store" as STORE
Developer -> SABLE : compare baseline and candidate IaC
SABLE -> HCL : parse baseline and candidate Terraform/HCL
HCL --> SABLE : resource graphs, moved blocks, parse status
SABLE -> BASE : load protected asset, principal, required actions
BASE --> SABLE : registered obligation / required-rule status
alt no trusted baseline resources
  SABLE -> STORE : record NOT_APPLICABLE (no continuity claim)
else required rules missing or parse / authority incomplete
  SABLE -> STORE : record UNKNOWN with reason
else baseline boundary available
  SABLE -> AUTH : verify baseline authorization satisfies obligation
  AUTH --> SABLE : verified / unverified baseline access
  alt baseline obligation not independently verified
    SABLE -> STORE : record UNKNOWN (baseline is not trusted)
  else baseline obligation verified
    SABLE -> CORR : identify protected resource successor
    CORR --> SABLE : ranked candidates, conflicts, confidence
    SABLE -> CORR : resolve moved principal only if unique
    CORR --> SABLE : candidate asset and principal / unresolved
    alt correspondence ambiguous or principal unresolved
      SABLE -> STORE : record UNKNOWN with correspondence reason
    else unique correspondence established
      SABLE -> AUTH : project candidate authorization for required actions
      AUTH --> SABLE : known / outside-model / holds / widening
      alt candidate semantics outside supported model
        SABLE -> STORE : record UNKNOWN with model boundary
      else obligation holds
        SABLE -> STORE : record PRESERVED evidence
      else obligation regressed
        SABLE -> STORE : record REGRESSED evidence
      end
    end
  end
end
SABLE --> Developer : findings + obligation trace
note over HCL,AUTH
Bounded local Terraform/HCL semantics for supported S3 and IAM
constructs; no deployed AWS state or universal Terraform coverage.
end note
@enduml
